<article class="env-lemma" id="0CZ2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CZ2">Lemma <span data-tag="0CZ2">67.45.11</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X_ i \to Y$, $i = 1, \ldots , n$ be finite morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $X_1 \amalg \ldots \amalg X_ n \to Y$ is finite too. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the case of schemes (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CYI" data-tag="0CYI">29.45.13</a>) by étale localization. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>